<Layout title="Our approach" description="The design philosophy behind Alder & Stone, a fictional landscaping business created for the SPR Web Studio portfolio."><section class="page-intro section"><p class="eyebrow">THE ALDER & STONE APPROACH</p><h1>A little more nature.<br/><em>A lot more intention.</em></h1><p>A fictional studio with a simple design philosophy: create outdoor spaces that feel connected to the people who use them.</p></section><div class="wide-photo"><Photo name="garden" alt="Garden inspiration with layered greenery" eager/></div><section class="section intro"><p class="eyebrow">THE PHILOSOPHY</p><div><h2>Not just a view.<br/><em>A way to live.</em></h2><p>Room for a morning coffee. A path that invites you to wander. A gathering space that keeps everyone outside a little longer. These everyday moments guide this sample brand.</p><p>Our concept balances soft planting with strong architectural elements. Natural texture, useful space, and a sense of belonging come before decoration.</p></div></section><section class="section values"><article><span class="eyebrow">01 / CONNECTION</span><h3>Start with the setting.</h3><p>Think about light, the home’s architecture, privacy, and how each outdoor room relates to the next.</p></article><article><span class="eyebrow">02 / MATERIALITY</span><h3>Let the materials speak.</h3><p>Use a restrained palette and let stone, wood, and planting create depth through their natural character.</p></article><article><span class="eyebrow">03 / EVERYDAY LIFE</span><h3>Make beauty useful.</h3><p>Consider access, maintenance, circulation, and changing seasons alongside the visual experience.</p></article></section><section class="section demo-explainer"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THIS WEBSITE</p><h2>A sample brand.<br/><em>A real design capability.</em></h2><p>Created by SPR Web Studio to demonstrate a premium landscaping website. Alder & Stone is a fictional business. There are no invented employees, client testimonials, awards, licenses, or completed projects here. Photographs are stock inspiration; project narratives are illustrative concepts.</p></section><CTA title="Imagine what your outdoors could be."/></Layout>
